# knobs_option_A.env -- CANDIDATE, NOT APPLIED. node arxiv-1902.10565::scale_data_window,
# obligation o47_rows_per_game_drift_rederive_at_17.
#
# OPTION A: keep the epoch at E = 20000 and buy freshness with more games.
# The ONLY change against codes/loop/knobs_9x9.env (sha256 3504a8ea9c9d0bfa9) is
# NUM_GAMES_PER_CYCLE 1500 -> 1800. Every other line is byte-identical to the live file.
#
# G is the solution of the same T1 inequality the live set solves, at the read-5 marginal
# and its 10-net drift bound, but demanded with a +20 % margin on the tolerance itself:
#   G >= 1.2 * (1.2*E) / r_lo = 28800 / 16.6532 = 1729.4  -> 1800 (rounded up to 100)
# and at the marginal itself 28800 / 17.7235 = 1624.9, so the drift bound binds.
# T1 then fails again only when the marginal falls to 1.2*E/G + 10*|slope|
#   = 24000/1800 + 1.070 = 14.403 rows/game, i.e. 31.0 accepted nets of headroom
# at the read-5 fitted slope -0.1070 (18.7 nets at o47's pessimistic -0.1528).
#
# At r = 15 the same +20 % rule gives G = 2100; at r = 13, G = 2500. Those are separate
# knob moves: option A must be re-derived at EVERY monitoring read that sees the marginal
# fall, which is exactly the ratchet o47 asks scale_data_window to replace.
#
# WHAT IT BUYS BESIDES T1: o47_options.md section 3 measures samples/cycle =
# SHUFFLE_KEEPROWS, so the reuse the loop really applies is rho = keep/(G*r); G 1500 -> 1800
# takes rho 4.51 -> 3.76 and the value head's samples per distinct game outcome 80 -> 66.7.
#
# COST: selfplay is 100 % of the added wall time. 3600*1800/6296.1 = 1029.2 s of selfplay
# per cycle against 857.7 s at 1500 (+20.0 %); the K7 model's whole cycle goes 1249 -> 1421 s
# (+13.7 %) and the storage write per cycle 15.13 -> 17.50 MiB (+15.7 %).
# Verify with:
#   python3 codes/eval/check_knobs_9x9.py \
#     --knobs evidence/scale_data_window/knobs_option_A.env \
#     --throughput evidence/production_chain/throughput.json \
#     --rows-file  evidence/production_chain/rows_per_game.txt \
#     --marginal-nets 3 --trend-nets 9 --horizon-nets 10

NUM_GAMES_PER_CYCLE=1800
NUM_THREADS_FOR_SHUFFLING=8
NUM_TRAIN_SAMPLES_PER_EPOCH=20000
MAX_TRAIN_PER_DATA=8
NUM_TRAIN_SAMPLES_PER_SWA=10000
BATCHSIZE=128
SHUFFLE_MINROWS=25000
MAX_TRAIN_SAMPLES_PER_CYCLE=100000
TAPER_WINDOW_SCALE=50000
SHUFFLE_KEEPROWS=120000
EPOCHS_PER_EXPORT=5
KTG_CPUS_PER_TASK=32
KTG_NUM_GAME_THREADS=18
